            "value" : "about %lld minutes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Almost all frames are from the same height (%lld° elevation spread). Cameras on a single ring give no vertical parallax, so top and bottom surfaces come out soft. Changing the phone's height/angle and shooting a second revolution is the single biggest improvement." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Almost all frames are from the same height (%lld° elevation spread). Cameras on a single ring give no vertical parallax, so top and bottom surfaces come out soft. Changing the phone's height/angle and shooting a second revolution is the single biggest improvement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Apple ecosystem, AR Quick Look. Source format — no conversion." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Apple ecosystem, AR Quick Look. Source format — no conversion."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "As the object turns, the light stays fixed relative to it. Shadows slide across the surface and the solver can't recognize the same point in two frames. Use diffuse light instead of a single lamp; if possible, rotate the lamp with the object." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "As the object turns, the light stays fixed relative to it. Shadows slide across the surface and the solver can't recognize the same point in two frames. Use diffuse light instead of a single lamp; if possible, rotate the lamp with the object."
          }
        }
      }
    },
